          "id": "e8c27c62-b056-45c4-bc59-ced452a50a41",
          "name": "Amazon Glue Get M L Task Runs",
          "request": {
            "name": "Amazon Glue Get M L Task Runs",
            "description": {
              "content": "<p>Gets a list of runs for a machine learning transform. Machine learning task runs are asynchronous tasks that Glue runs on your behalf as part of various machine learning workflows. You can get a sortable, filterable list of machine learning task runs by calling <code>GetMLTaskRuns</code> with their parent transform's <code>TransformID</code> and other optional parameters as documented in this section.</p> <p>This operation returns a list of historic runs and must be paginated.</p>",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                ""
              ],
              "hash": "X-Amz-Target=AWSGlue.GetMLTaskRuns",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "MaxResults",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "Pagination limit"
                },
